<!-- LEARNINGS -->
<section class="case-section">
  <h2>What I'd do again.</h2>
  <div class="copy">
    <p><strong>Pick the app's backbone from the business, not the screens.</strong> Building everything off "projects" and "communities" meant search, offers and updates all reused one card and one detail page instead of each becoming its own mini-app.</p>
    <p><strong>Ask for language before anything else.</strong> Making it the first screen forced every layout to be designed in both directions from the start — far cheaper than retrofitting RTL after the LTR screens were signed off.</p>
    <p><strong>Give "following a project" a payoff.</strong> Dated construction updates plus push turned a brochure app into something a buyer opens again next month.</p>
  </div>
</section>

